Subject: [PATCH] rpmsg: use channel aliases for nodes without compatible

An RPMsg channel can have a firmware node for channel properties without
an OF compatible. The OF modalias helper still succeeds for these nodes,
producing a name-only alias that does not match the RPMsg driver ID table.

Use the OF alias only when a compatible property exists. Otherwise retain
the ordinary RPMsg channel alias, allowing services such as QRTR to load
through their existing module aliases. OF-compatible channels and error
handling keep their current behavior.

---
--- a/drivers/rpmsg/rpmsg_core.c
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/rpmsg_core.c
@@ -417,9 +417,11 @@
 	const struct rpmsg_device *rpdev = to_rpmsg_device(dev);
 	int ret;
 
-	ret = of_device_uevent_modalias(dev, env);
-	if (ret != -ENODEV)
-		return ret;
+	if (of_property_present(dev->of_node, "compatible")) {
+		ret = of_device_uevent_modalias(dev, env);
+		if (ret != -ENODEV)
+			return ret;
+	}
 
 	return add_uevent_var(env, "MODALIAS=" RPMSG_DEVICE_MODALIAS_FMT,
 					rpdev->id.name);
